      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "border_crossing_scene",
      "label": "Immigration Policy Context",
      "description": "The image of migrants crossing a border is a common visual trope in political discourse, often used to represent illegal immigration. The meme uses this scene to imply that the migrants have 'no right to be here,' which is a politically charged claim that requires understanding of U.S. immigration law and policy debates.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
